WEBVTT

cue-1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.300
In Bellweather, every train followed the station clock.

cue-2
00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:07.633
Nobody remembered who had decided that the clock should be trusted.

cue-3
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.800
At eleven each night, the last train crossed the river.

cue-4
00:00:11.967 --> 00:00:16.567
Its windows passed the clockmaker’s workshop like a row of little suns.

cue-5
00:00:17.333 --> 00:00:20.233
Then one Tuesday, the whistle did not come.

cue-6
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:24.933
The workshop clocks kept ticking, but the river outside remained dark.

cue-7
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.067
The timetable promised a train.

cue-8
00:00:28.233 --> 00:00:31.200
The station clock insisted it was early.

cue-9
00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:34.033
Both could not describe the same moment.

cue-10
00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:37.333
Mara opened her father’s old drawer.

cue-11
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:43.233
Inside lay a silver pocket watch, a red ribbon, and a key with one broken tooth.

cue-12
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.200
The pocket watch said eleven.

cue-13
00:00:46.367 --> 00:00:51.433
Mara had wound it that morning, using the noon bell from the hill above town.

cue-14
00:00:52.167 --> 00:00:54.800
A clock, a timetable, and a watch.

cue-15
00:00:54.967 --> 00:00:59.500
Mara placed them side by side, looking for the one that disagreed.

cue-16
00:01:00.233 --> 00:01:03.233
She followed the rails through the sleeping town.

cue-17
00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:07.767
At the bridge, a red signal burned above a perfectly empty track.

cue-18
00:01:08.533 --> 00:01:11.167
Beyond the bend, the train was waiting.

cue-19
00:01:11.333 --> 00:01:16.267
Steam slipped from its wheels, and the driver pointed toward the signal tower.

cue-20
00:01:17.033 --> 00:01:19.400
Nothing was wrong with the engine.

cue-21
00:01:19.567 --> 00:01:24.900
The automatic signal refused to open until the station clock reached eleven.

cue-22
00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:28.100
One clock controlled one signal.

cue-23
00:01:28.267 --> 00:01:30.700
One signal controlled the bridge.

cue-24
00:01:30.867 --> 00:01:34.967
An entire journey depended on a single delayed instruction.

cue-25
00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:38.000
Mara climbed into the tower.

cue-26
00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:45.133
Behind the enormous dial, she found gears turning with the solemn confidence of something already believed.

cue-27
00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:48.867
A tiny wheel slipped once each revolution.

cue-28
00:01:49.033 --> 00:01:53.967
The clock was losing minutes while everything downstream continued to obey it.

cue-29
00:01:54.767 --> 00:01:56.367
The fault was small.

cue-30
00:01:56.533 --> 00:01:58.500
Its consequence was not.

cue-31
00:01:58.667 --> 00:02:03.533
Repeating the same small error had pushed the whole railway behind the night.

cue-32
00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:06.600
Mara could force the hands forward.

cue-33
00:02:06.767 --> 00:02:11.867
But moving the hands would hide the fault, and tomorrow the delay would return.

cue-34
00:02:12.633 --> 00:02:14.633
She took out the broken key.

cue-35
00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:20.133
Its missing tooth matched a notch in a small service hatch beneath the slipping wheel.

cue-36
00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:23.533
The hatch opened onto a spare wheel.

cue-37
00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:29.200
Her father had left the part where only somebody investigating the fault would find it.

cue-38
00:02:29.967 --> 00:02:32.467
The spare wheel was not a shortcut.

cue-39
00:02:32.633 --> 00:02:37.433
It was an invitation to fix the cause instead of adjusting the appearance.

cue-40
00:02:38.233 --> 00:02:40.300
Mara stopped the mechanism.

cue-41
00:02:40.467 --> 00:02:44.833
For the first time in her life, the tower was silent enough to hear the river.

cue-42
00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:48.700
She replaced the slipping wheel and checked the fit.

cue-43
00:02:48.867 --> 00:02:52.600
Tooth met tooth, and the mechanism turned without a stumble.

cue-44
00:02:53.367 --> 00:02:57.433
Before restarting the signal, she compared the tower with her watch.

cue-45
00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:01.667
Agreement mattered more than the authority of the larger dial.

cue-46
00:03:02.433 --> 00:03:04.833
At last, the bridge signal changed.

cue-47
00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:09.667
Green light fell onto the rails, and the waiting train answered with a whistle.

cue-48
00:03:10.433 --> 00:03:12.967
Mara watched the windows cross the river.

cue-49
00:03:13.133 --> 00:03:18.300
Behind each one was somebody whose evening had been waiting for a tiny wheel.

cue-50
00:03:19.067 --> 00:03:22.267
Inside the wrapping, her father had left a note.

cue-51
00:03:22.433 --> 00:03:26.133
Trust a clock, it said, only after you have checked another.

cue-52
00:03:26.867 --> 00:03:30.367
The following morning, Mara installed a second clock.

cue-53
00:03:30.533 --> 00:03:35.267
It used a separate mechanism and faced the people waiting on the platform.

cue-54
00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:39.367
Bellweather did not become a town without mistakes.

cue-55
00:03:39.533 --> 00:03:43.100
It became a town with one more way to notice them.

cue-56
00:03:43.867 --> 00:03:46.833
Mara kept the silver watch beside her tools.

cue-57
00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:51.567
The red ribbon marked its place, and the broken key stayed in the drawer.

cue-58
00:03:52.333 --> 00:03:54.967
That night, the last train crossed on time.

cue-59
00:03:55.133 --> 00:03:59.433
Mara heard its whistle, looked at both clocks, and went back to work.
